                "text": "A freestanding ER like ER of White Rock is a fully equipped emergency room that operates independently from a hospital. It has experienced ER physicians, on-site CT scanners, digital X-ray, and full lab capabilities available 24/7. Urgent care centers handle minor illnesses and injuries but cannot treat life-threatening emergencies, perform advanced imaging, or provide the level of care a freestanding ER can."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How long is the wait time at ER of White Rock?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "ER of White Rock is designed for minimal wait times. Our patients are seen quickly by an experienced emergency physician. We are open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, so you receive fast, attentive care regardless of when you arrive."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What conditions should I go to the ER for?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "You should visit ER of White Rock for serious or life-threatening conditions including chest pain, difficulty breathing, severe abdominal pain, stroke symptoms, broken bones, head injuries, high fever, severe allergic reactions, and deep cuts requiring stitches. If you are unsure, it is always safer to come in and get evaluated by one of our emergency physicians."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does ER of White Rock treat children?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. ER of White Rock provides 24/7 pediatric emergency care for infants, children, and teenagers. Our experienced emergency physicians treat pediatric emergencies including high fevers, dehydration, injuries, allergic reactions, and respiratory issues in a comfortable and compassionate environment."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Where is ER of White Rock located and how do I get there?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "ER of White Rock is located at 10705 Northwest Hwy, Dallas, TX 75238, conveniently serving White Rock Lake, Lake Highlands, Casa View, East Dallas, and surrounding neighborhoods. Free parking is available on-site. Walk in anytime, no appointment needed."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does ER of White Rock accept insurance?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. ER of White Rock accepts most major commercial insurance plans as well as cash and credit cards. Our staff can help clarify your coverage and financial options when you arrive."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is ER of White Rock open 24 hours?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. ER of White Rock is open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year, including all holidays. Emergencies do not follow a schedule, and neither do we."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Do I need an appointment to visit ER of White Rock?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No appointment is needed. Simply walk in anytime and you will be seen by an experienced emergency physician. ER of White Rock is always open and ready to provide immediate emergency care."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
