    "text": "24/7 Emergency Room in White Rock, TXAt ER of White Rock, our experienced emergency physicians and trauma-trained nurses are ready around the clock to provide immediate, hospital-level care for adults and children, right here close to home.We are your neighborhood emergency room, located just minutes from White Rock Lake, Lake Highlands, and Casa View. Walk in any time, day or night, and you will be seen quickly by a specialist who is focused entirely on you. Call Now Get Direction Minimal Wait Time We prioritize your health with efficient triage systems designed to get you from the door to a physician in minutes, not hours. Experienced Emergency Physicians Our team consists of specialists trained in emergency medicine, providing the same level of care as a major hospital with a personal touch. On-Site Advanced Imaging Equipped with the latest CT scans, X-rays, and full laboratory services for rapid and accurate diagnosis on the spot.Comprehensive Emergency Services View all services Chest Pain & Stroke CareWe provide expert emergency care for chest pain and stroke to ensure rapid diagnosis and treatment.Broken Bones & FracturesGet immediate care for fractures and broken bones at ER of White Rock with advanced treatment options.Pediatric EmergenciesReceive compassionate and specialized emergency care from our expert team for children of all ages.Severe Allergic ReactionsWe offer fast and effective treatment for life-threatening allergic reactions to ensure quick relief and recovery.Head Injuries & ConcussionsOur doctors provide expert diagnosis and treatment for head injuries and concussions to prevent further complications.Diagnostic ImagingAdvanced diagnostic services are available at ER of White Rock for quick and accurate results.Why White Rock and Lake Highlands Families Choose Us Open 24 Hours a Day, Every Day of the Year We never close. Whether it is a Tuesday afternoon or a holiday at 3 in the morning, our full emergency care team is on-site and ready to treat you. Experienced Physicians and Trauma-Trained Nurses Every physician on our team holds board certification in emergency medicine. Our nursing staff is trained in trauma care and pediatric emergencies. Advanced Imaging and Laboratory Services On-Site Our facility is equipped with CT scanners, digital X-ray, and a COLA-certified laboratory. Results are available quickly, so treatment begins without delay. Transparent and Affordable Pricing We accept most major insurance plans and offer discounted self-pay rates. Our pricing is clear and straightforward from the start. Pediatric Emergency Care in White RockWhen your child is hurting, every second counts. You need more than just an emergency room. You need a team that understands the unique physiological and emotional needs of children. ER of White Rock provides specialized pediatric care in a calm, kid-friendly environment designed to reduce anxiety for both patients and parents.Why Choose ER of White Rock for Your Child?Our facility bridges the gap between clinical excellence and compassionate care. We prioritize your child’s comfort through:Pediatric Specialists: Our physicians and nurses are trained specifically in pediatric emergency protocols.Child-Centered Environment: A clean, quiet, and less intimidating atmosphere than traditional city hospitals.Clear Communication: We skip the medical jargon. You get honest answers and a clear plan of action.Family-First Approach: We keep you involved and informed at every stage of the treatment process.Advanced On-Site DiagnosticsAnswers in Minutes, Not HoursOur laboratory is COLA-certified, meeting the highest national standards for clinical testing excellence. Full Lab Digital X-Ray Multi-Slice CT EKG & Cardiac When Should You Go to the Emergency Room?Seek immediate emergency care for any life-threatening symptoms, including: Difficulty breathing or severe shortness of breath Signs of stroke (facial drooping, slurred speech) Uncontrolled bleeding or deep lacerations Sudden, severe pain or high fever Chest pain, pressure, or radiating arm pain Loss of consciousness or severe confusion Severe burns or poisoning Major fractures or head trauma A Proud Member of NAFEC and TAFEC Serving Our CommunityWe are proud to serve families across East Dallas and the surrounding metroplex: White Rock Lake Highlands Casa View Lakewood Forest Hills Garland Mesquite East DallasInsurance, Self-Pay and Transparent BillingWe believe high-end medical care should be accessible and transparent. We honor all private insurance plans (Aetna, BlueCross BlueShield, Cigna, United Healthcare, etc.) at in-network rates for emergency services, per Texas law. Disclaimer: By law, freestanding emergency centers cannot accept Medicaid, Medicare, or TRICARE. We apologize for any inconvenience. Find Us - Right Off Northwest HighwayMinutes from White Rock Lake and centrally located for Lake Highlands residents. Address 10705 Northwest Hwy, Dallas, TX 75238, United States Phone (469) 943-2939 Hours Open 24 Hours / 7 Days a Week Frequently Asked QuestionsCommon questions about the ER of White Rock: What is the difference between a freestanding ER and an urgent care? A freestanding ER like ER of White Rock is a fully equipped emergency room that operates independently from a hospital. It has experienced ER physicians, on-site CT scanners, digital X-ray, and full lab capabilities available 24/7. Urgent care centers handle minor illnesses and injuries but cannot treat life-threatening emergencies, perform advanced imaging, or provide the level of care a freestanding ER can. How long is the wait time at ER of White Rock? ER of White Rock is designed for minimal wait times. Our patients are seen quickly by an experienced emergency physician. We are open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, so you receive fast, attentive care regardless of when you arrive. What conditions should I go to the ER for? You should visit ER of White Rock for serious or life-threatening conditions including chest pain, difficulty breathing, severe abdominal pain, stroke symptoms, broken bones, head injuries, high fever, severe allergic reactions, and deep cuts requiring stitches. If you are unsure, it is always safer to come in and get evaluated by one of our emergency physicians. Does ER of White Rock treat children? Yes. ER of White Rock provides 24/7 pediatric emergency care for infants, children, and teenagers. Our experienced emergency physicians treat pediatric emergencies including high fevers, dehydration, injuries, allergic reactions, and respiratory issues in a comfortable and compassionate environment. Where is ER of White Rock located and how do I get there? ER of White Rock is located at 10705 Northwest Hwy, Dallas, TX 75238, conveniently serving White Rock Lake, Lake Highlands, Casa View, East Dallas, and surrounding neighborhoods. Free parking is available on-site. Walk in anytime, no appointment needed. Does ER of White Rock accept insurance? Yes. ER of White Rock accepts most major commercial insurance plans as well as cash and credit cards. Our staff can help clarify your coverage and financial options when you arrive. Is ER of White Rock open 24 hours? Yes. ER of White Rock is open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year, including all holidays. Emergencies do not follow a schedule, and neither do we. Do I need an appointment to visit ER of White Rock? No appointment is needed. Simply walk in anytime and you will be seen by an experienced emergency physician. ER of White Rock is always open and ready to provide immediate emergency care. Latest Insights What to Tell the ER Team: A Medication and Symptom Note Read More » How Long Does an ER Visit Take? A Step by Step Look at the Timeline Read More » Hit Your Head? When to Go to the ER and When to Watch at Home Read More »",
